        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does oil tank replacement cost in Dieppe?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Most standard above-ground replacements in Dieppe land between $2,500 and $4,500 CAD, depending on the tank type, where it sits, and how much oil needs transferring. You'll always get a free written estimate before any work starts. Our cost guide covers what pushes a job toward either end of that range.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">My insurer wants proof my tank was replaced. How fast can you get to Dieppe?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Usually within a day or two for the estimate, since Dieppe is only minutes from our Moncton base. Most replacements can be booked within the same week. Every job comes with dated paperwork you can send straight to your insurance company.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">We speak French at home. Is that a problem?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Not at all. A lot of our Dieppe customers are French-first, and that's never been an issue on a job. Our estimates and paperwork are written in plain English, and we'll gladly walk through every line with you until it all makes sense.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">Could my older Dieppe home have a buried oil tank?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">If your house dates from the 1950s to the 1970s in a neighbourhood like Saint-Anselme or Chartersville, it's possible. Telltale signs include a fill or vent pipe in the yard that doesn't connect to anything obvious, or a faint oil smell after heavy rain. We can locate the tank, remove it, and document the site properly.</p>
      </div>
